From 0a2b7c48a84bec5f02a37f2d8f77074a7c0847ec Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 04:40:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Sleep timer: quiet re-check while paused, read the queue only
 as far as needed

A boundary timer that expired while paused re-armed itself for the unchanged remaining
time, broadcasting a player update each time (twice a second near a boundary). Paused,
it now checks back every 5 s without telling clients; stopped playback ends the timer.
The queue is read lazily: track end looks at one item, album end until the album ends,
fit until the time budget runs out.

